<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Acts of Union 1707</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1707">1707</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Acts of Union</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Acts of Union 1707 were the parliamentary acts that united the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Kingdom of Great Britain</a> in 1707. They created a single parliament and a common market, opening English colonial trade to Scots. The union is treated as a foundational step for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/acts-of-union-1707.jpg" alt="Acts of Union 1707" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_England_(1702%E2%80%931707).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
